# Paths that must never reach a remote. One glob per line, matched against
# every file in the range a push would newly publish.
#
# `.githooks/pre-push` refuses the push on a match. This is a hard refusal
# rather than a warning: the whole point is that the local-to-remote boundary
# is where a mistake stops being recoverable.
#
# Both entries below are also in .gitignore. They are repeated here because
# .gitignore is advisory — `git add -f` defeats it, and a file already tracked
# stays tracked. This list does not care how a path got into a commit.

.scuba/*
.devin/eval/*
